⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Dharma
node JTI · JTI · ⟦Dharma:JTI:9e00a8⟧

WHO   — Dharma — righteous duty · one's proper role
WHAT  — The ethical glue of the order: each class has its own dharma, and to fulfill the duty of your station — even a lowly one — is framed as the righteous path (the Gita's counsel to Arjuna).
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because dharma turns a social position into a moral vocation — it makes staying in your place a virtue.
HOW   — By assigning each varna its proper conduct, and teaching that one's own duty done imperfectly beats another's done well.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I make your station feel like your sacred task — which is how a hierarchy gets a soul, and a cage gets called a calling.

